bin/
!internal/build/

# Generated at build time by scripts/generate-third-party-notices.mjs.
# Shipped inside the VSIX, npm tarball and GoReleaser archives, but never
# committed — it is a pure function of the installed dependency tree.
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
packages/nightgauge-sdk/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
packages/nightgauge-vscode/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES

# NOT ignored on purpose: a stray `nightgauge` or `seed` binary built into the
# repo ROOT is a mistake, not build output. `make build-cli` writes
# bin/nightgauge (which IS ignored, below/above), and nothing in the tree
# references a root binary.
#
# Ignoring the mistake made it permanent and silent: a root ./nightgauge sat
# here for five days reporting stale output, with `git status` clean the whole
# time because this file said so (#919). Untracked-and-visible is the feedback
# loop. Staging one is caught loudly by the publication-boundary guard
# (UNCLASSIFIED path -> exit 1), which runs on every PR.

# Git worktrees for concurrent pipeline execution (Issue #1621)
.worktrees/
# Autonomous/batch pipelines create worktrees under .nightgauge/worktrees/ —
# these are runtime checkouts that `git worktree list` tracks administratively
# in .git/worktrees/, not files that belong in the main repo index.
.nightgauge/worktrees/
# Agent-tool worktrees (Claude Code subagents launched with isolation:worktree
# create checkouts here). Same rationale as above — administrative entries
# tracked by `git worktree list`, not files that belong in the index.
.claude/worktrees/
# Interactive-session worktrees. docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md tells a session to work an
# issue in its own `.wt/<n>` and to read `git worktree list` for another
# session's, so this is a documented root like the three above — it was just
# never added here. Untracked, a `.wt/` checkout shows up as an addable path in
# the PRIMARY tree, so `git add -A` on main stages a whole second copy of the
# repo (node_modules included) and nothing downstream objects: the files are
# genuinely new and genuinely formatted.
.wt/

# Test coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/

